<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The agent owner — a job of its own, and that is the whole point.

  Agents started from the fleet screen live on ptys this process holds. It is
  deliberately NOT started by the dashboard: a process started by the dashboard
  shares the dashboard's fate, which is the defect (CB-1) the owner exists to
  remove. The installer places this file; nothing else will, and without it the
  fleet screen's start control is dead.

  Measured on macOS 2026-08-27: an agent forked onto a pty leads its own session
  and survives `launchctl kickstart -k`, `kill -9` and `unload` of the job that
  started it. A child sharing the job's session does not — so this job's own
  restart takes nothing with it except the terminals it was holding, which end
  with the pty master whatever the platform.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>com.set-core.agent-owner</string>
  <!--
    The wrapper, not the module file. `bin/set-agent-owner` execs
    `python -m set_orch.fleet.ownerd`, and the `-m` is load-bearing: `ownerd.py`
    uses package-relative imports and dies on `from . import scopes` when run as
    a path. Measured 2026-08-27 — the first version of this plist named the file
    and the job exited 1 on every launch, which reads from the fleet screen as
    "the owner is not running" with no clue why. The systemd unit invokes the
    same wrapper, so the two cannot drift.

    No `--socket`: the systemd unit passes `%t/set-agent-owner.sock` because that
    is what its `%t` expands to, and there is no macOS equivalent to hardcode.
    Leaving it off lets the resolver in `ownerd.default_socket_path()` answer for
    the platform, which is the one place that decision lives.
  -->
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>__INSTALL_DIR__/set-agent-owner</string>
    <string>serve</string>
  </array>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PYTHONPATH</key><string>__SET_TOOLS_ROOT__/lib:__SET_TOOLS_ROOT__/modules/web</string>
    <key>PATH</key><string>__INSTALL_DIR__:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin</string>
  </dict>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><true/>
  <key>KeepAlive</key><true/>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>__LOG_DIR__/set-agent-owner.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>__LOG_DIR__/set-agent-owner.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
